From: FastFlow SDK <fastflow-sdk@amd.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bind HRX sub-buffers at their byte offset

IRON's Gemma 4 override builds an XRT-style sub-buffer, bo(parent, size,
offset), and keys views on get_handle().get(). HRX dispatches bind that
slice at its byte offset. Host and device dirty state is a set of ranges,
so one slice does not clear a disjoint slice of the same allocation. A
failed flush or invalidate records that range again and still applies the
ranges after it. A slice that extends past its parent is rejected.
